  "id": "elections-08-electing-your-member-of-parliament",
  "chapter": "Federal Elections",
  "order": 8,
  "title": {
    "en": "Electing your member of Parliament",
    "fr": "Élire votre député"
  },
  "passages": [
    {
      "id": "e8-what-canadians-vote-for",
      "text": {
        "en": "In an election, Canadians vote for the people they want to speak for them in the House of Commons.",
        "fr": "Lors d'une élection, les Canadiens votent pour les personnes qu'ils veulent voir parler en leur nom à la Chambre des communes."
      },
      "fact": {
        "factual": true,
        "source": {
          "sourceId": "discover-canada",
          "chapter": "Federal Elections",
          "page": 60,
          "url": "https://www.canada.ca/en/immigration-refugees-citizenship/corporate/publications-manuals/discover-canada.html",
          "sourceHash": "fd51046981916115cc39b989e9eedd3ab2c5943aeb7e0fe4e237e13a0da7c836",
          "asOf": "2026-09-08T00:00:00Z",
          "volatile": true,
          "quote": "Canadians vote in elections for the people they want to represent them in the House of Commons."
        },
        "verification": {
          "status": "unverified",
          "model": "",
          "checkedAt": null,
          "sourceHash": "",
          "evidence": ""
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e8-re-elect-or-choose-new",
      "text": {
        "en": "At each election, voters can send the same members back to the House of Commons, or they can pick new ones.",
        "fr": "À chaque élection, les électeurs peuvent renvoyer les mêmes députés à la Chambre des communes ou en choisir de nouveaux."
      },
      "fact": {
        "factual": true,
        "source": {
          "sourceId": "discover-canada",
          "chapter": "Federal Elections",
          "page": 60,
          "url": "https://www.canada.ca/en/immigration-refugees-citizenship/corporate/publications-manuals/discover-canada.html",
          "sourceHash": "fd51046981916115cc39b989e9eedd3ab2c5943aeb7e0fe4e237e13a0da7c836",
          "asOf": "2026-09-08T00:00:00Z",
          "volatile": true,
          "quote": "In each election, voters may re-elect the same members of the House of Commons or choose new ones."
        },
        "verification": {
          "status": "unverified",
          "model": "",
          "checkedAt": null,
          "sourceHash": "",
          "evidence": ""
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e8-fixed-election-date",
      "text": {
        "en": "A law passed by Parliament sets the date of federal elections. One must be held on the third Monday of October, four years after the last general election.",
        "fr": "Une loi adoptée par le Parlement fixe la date des élections fédérales. Une élection doit avoir lieu le troisième lundi d'octobre, quatre ans après la dernière élection générale."
      },
      "fact": {
        "factual": true,
        "source": {
          "sourceId": "discover-canada",
          "chapter": "Federal Elections",
          "page": 60,
          "url": "https://www.canada.ca/en/immigration-refugees-citizenship/corporate/publications-manuals/discover-canada.html",
          "sourceHash": "fd51046981916115cc39b989e9eedd3ab2c5943aeb7e0fe4e237e13a0da7c836",
          "asOf": "2026-09-08T00:00:00Z",
          "volatile": true,
          "quote": "Under legislation passed by Parliament, federal elections must be held on the third Monday in October every four years following the most recent general election."
        },
        "verification": {
          "status": "unverified",
          "model": "",
          "checkedAt": null,
          "sourceHash": "",
          "evidence": ""
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e8-an-earlier-election",
      "text": {
        "en": "The Prime Minister can ask the Governor General to call an election sooner than that.",
        "fr": "Le premier ministre peut demander au gouverneur général de déclencher une élection plus tôt."
      },
      "fact": {
        "factual": true,
        "source": {
          "sourceId": "discover-canada",
          "chapter": "Federal Elections",
          "page": 60,
          "url": "https://www.canada.ca/en/immigration-refugees-citizenship/corporate/publications-manuals/discover-canada.html",
          "sourceHash": "fd51046981916115cc39b989e9eedd3ab2c5943aeb7e0fe4e237e13a0da7c836",
          "asOf": "2026-09-08T00:00:00Z",
          "volatile": true,
          "quote": "The Prime Minister may ask the Governor General to call an earlier election."
        },
        "verification": {
          "status": "unverified",
          "model": "",
          "checkedAt": null,
          "sourceHash": "",
          "evidence": ""
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e8-ridings-and-constituencies",
      "text": {
        "en": "Canada is split into electoral districts. People also call them ridings or constituencies.",
        "fr": "Le Canada est divisé en circonscriptions électorales. On les appelle aussi des comtés, ou tout simplement des circonscriptions."
      },
      "fact": {
        "factual": true,
        "source": {
          "sourceId": "discover-canada",
          "chapter": "Federal Elections",
          "page": 60,
          "url": "https://www.canada.ca/en/immigration-refugees-citizenship/corporate/publications-manuals/discover-canada.html",
          "sourceHash": "fd51046981916115cc39b989e9eedd3ab2c5943aeb7e0fe4e237e13a0da7c836",
          "asOf": "2026-09-08T00:00:00Z",
          "volatile": true,
          "quote": "electoral districts, also known as ridings or constituencies."
        },
        "verification": {
          "status": "unverified",
          "model": "",
          "checkedAt": null,
          "sourceHash": "",
          "evidence": ""
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e8-what-an-electoral-district-is",
      "text": {
        "en": "An electoral district is an area on the map. A member of Parliament (MP) represents it.",
        "fr": "Une circonscription électorale est un territoire délimité sur la carte. Un député la représente."
      },
      "fact": {
        "factual": true,
        "source": {
          "sourceId": "discover-canada",
          "chapter": "Federal Elections",
          "page": 60,
          "url": "https://www.canada.ca/en/immigration-refugees-citizenship/corporate/publications-manuals/discover-canada.html",
          "sourceHash": "fd51046981916115cc39b989e9eedd3ab2c5943aeb7e0fe4e237e13a0da7c836",
          "asOf": "2026-09-08T00:00:00Z",
          "volatile": true,
          "quote": "An electoral district is a geographical area represented by a member of Parliament (MP)."
        },
        "verification": {
          "status": "unverified",
          "model": "",
          "checkedAt": null,
          "sourceHash": "",
          "evidence": ""
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e8-whom-an-mp-represents",
      "text": {
        "en": "The citizens of each electoral district elect one MP. That MP sits in the House of Commons and speaks for them, and for all Canadians too.",
        "fr": "Les citoyens de chaque circonscription élisent un député. Ce député siège à la Chambre des communes et les représente, ainsi que tous les Canadiens."
      },
      "fact": {
        "factual": true,
        "source": {
          "sourceId": "discover-canada",
          "chapter": "Federal Elections",
          "page": 60,
          "url": "https://www.canada.ca/en/immigration-refugees-citizenship/corporate/publications-manuals/discover-canada.html",
          "sourceHash": "fd51046981916115cc39b989e9eedd3ab2c5943aeb7e0fe4e237e13a0da7c836",
          "asOf": "2026-09-08T00:00:00Z",
          "volatile": true,
          "quote": "The citizens in each electoral district elect one MP who sits in the House of Commons to represent them, as well as all Canadians."
        },
        "verification": {
          "status": "unverified",
          "model": "",
          "checkedAt": null,
          "sourceHash": "",
          "evidence": ""
        }
      }
    },
    {
